   "x": 60,
   "y": 60,
   "text": "Example: RS422 – one master (SQ1) and two slaves (SQ2, SQ3), 4-wire full duplex, 600 m",
   "size": 18,
   "bold": 1,
   "it": 0,
   "al": "left",
   "rot": 0
  },
  {
   "id": 202,
   "k": "text",
   "pg": 1,
   "all": 0,
   "col": "",
   "wd": 2,
   "ds": "",
   "x": 60,
   "y": 78,
   "text": "Press Run. Top trace = what the device sends (pair TX+ / TX−), bottom trace = what arrives. The master sends every slot, the slaves answer in turn. Use Serial Viewer in Properties.",
   "size": 12,
   "bold": 0,
   "it": 0,
   "al": "left",
   "rot": 0
  },
  {
   "id": 203,
   "k": "text",
   "pg": 1,
   "all": 0,
   "col": "",
   "wd": 2,
   "ds": "",
   "x": 60,
   "y": 96,
   "text": "Wiring: master TX+/TX− → RX+/RX− of both slaves; TX+/TX− of both slaves → RX+/RX− of the master; GND to GND. Termination ON at the last slave (SQ3) and the master.",
   "size": 12,
   "bold": 0,
   "it": 0,
   "al": "left",
   "rot": 0
  },
  {
   "id": 204,
   "k": "text",
   "pg": 1,
   "all": 0,
   "col": "",
   "wd": 2,
   "ds": "",
   "x": 60,
   "y": 114,
   "text": "Break it: give SQ3 another baud rate or parity, swap TX+/TX− on SQ2, switch the termination off at 1000 m and 115200 baud, or set a second device to Master.",
   "size": 12,
   "bold": 0,
   "it": 0,
   "al": "left",
   "rot": 0
  }
